/*!
    \example raycaster
    \ingroup quick3dphysics-examples
    \title Qt Quick 3D Physics - Raycaster Example
    \examplecategory {3D}
    \brief Demonstrates continuous ray intersection queries using Raycaster.
    \image raycaster-example.webp {Raycaster intersecting physics bodies}

    The example sweeps a \l Raycaster across a static box, a dynamic sphere, and
    the floor. The ray changes color when it reports an intersection, and a yellow
    marker shows the scene-space \l {locationHit::position}{hit position}.

    \section1 Configuring the Ray

    The Raycaster is a child of a semi-transparent dynamic body. Its
    \l {Raycaster::excludeParentBody}{excludeParentBody} property determines
    whether that body can be reported as the closest hit:

    \snippet raycaster/Main.qml raycast

    The control panel enables or disables the ray, selects static and dynamic
    bodies, and changes the maximum query distance. Two controls leave bodies
    out of the result: one toggles parent exclusion, and one names the blue
    sphere in \l {Raycaster::excludedBodies}{excludedBodies}, so the ray passes
    through it and reports the floor instead. The sweep can also be paused to
    set the ray angle manually:

    \snippet raycaster/Main.qml controls
*/
